      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Advanced geometry on the EST II includes angle theorems, triangle congruence and similarity, and properties of quadrilaterals and regular polygons.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Triangle angle sum",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( 180^\\circ \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Polygon angle sum",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( (n-2)\\times 180^\\circ \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Area of triangle",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\tfrac{1}{2}bh \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Law of cosines",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( c^2=a^2+b^2-2ab\\cos C \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 4.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "In triangle \\( ABC \\), \\( a=7 \\), \\( b=10 \\), \\( C=60^\\circ \\). Find \\( c \\). \\[ c^2=49+100-2(7)(10)\\cos 60^\\circ=149-70=79,\\quad c=\\sqrt{79}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Lines, Triangles & Polygons",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Parallel lines cut by a transversal: alternate interior angles are equal; co-interior (same-side) angles are supplementary. <strong>Triangle congruence:</strong> SSS, SAS, ASA, AAS, RHS. <strong>Similarity:</strong> AA, SAS, SSS — corresponding sides proportional. Exterior angle = sum of two non-adjacent interior angles.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Exterior angle theorem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "In triangle \\(ABC\\), \\(\\angle A = 48°\\) and \\(\\angle B = 63°\\). Find the exterior angle at \\(C\\). <p>Exterior angle \\(= \\angle A + \\angle B = 48° + 63° = 111°\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Two sides of a triangle are 7 cm and 10 cm with an included angle of 90°. Find the hypotenuse and all angles.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(c = \\sqrt{49+100} = \\sqrt{149} \\approx 12.2\\) cm. \\(\\tan A = 7/10 \\Rightarrow A \\approx 35.0°\\). \\(B \\approx 55.0°\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
